uctured_base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io'\\n  - gemini_model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash'\\n  - match_threshold: float = 0.75 (minimum similarity for candidate matching)\\n- Function load_config() that reads from .env and returns Config\\n- Raises clear error if required keys are missing\\n\\n## 6. src/extract/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 7. src/extract/excel_reader.py\\nModule to read Excel files (both shortages and warehouse lists):\\n- Function read_excel(filepath: Path) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Opens the Excel file with openpyxl\\n  - Auto-detects which sheet has data (skip empty sheets)\\n  - Auto-detects header row (first row with multiple non-empty cells)\\n  - Returns list of dicts with column headers as keys\\n  - Preserves all original values as-is (strings, numbers)\\n  - Handles both Arabic and English column names\\n- Function extract_item_names(rows: list[dict], name_column: str = None) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - If name_column is provided, use it\\n  - Otherwise, auto-detect the column most likely to contain drug names (look for columns with Arabic text, keywords like 'صنف', 'اسم', 'دواء')\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_row\\\": int, \\\"source_file\\\": str}\\n  - Keeps ALL original text including abbreviations, numbers, etc.\\n\\n## 8. src/extract/pdf_reader.py\\nModule to extract drug names from PDF files using Unstructured API:\\n- Function extract_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> dict that:\\n  - Uploads PDF to Unstructured API with profile='best', output='elements'\\n  - Handles polling for async jobs (status checking loop)\\n  - Returns the full JSON response\\n  - Saves the raw response to a .json file alongside the PDF\\n\\n- Function parse_items_from_response(response: dict) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - First checks if 'extracted_data' has items (from Extract step)\\n  - If not, looks for Table elements with text_as_html and parses the HTML tables\\n  - If no structured tables, falls back to parsing the text content\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_page\\\": int|None}\\n\\n- Function extract_items_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Calls extract_from_pdf to get the response\\n  - Then calls parse_items_from_response\\n  - Adds source_file to each item\\n  - Returns the final list\\n\\nFor the HTML table parsing, use a simple approach:\\n- Parse the text_as_html field from Table elements\\n- Find the column that contains drug names (usually the second column after a code column, or the column with Arabic text)\\n- Extract each row's drug name cell\\n\\nIMPORTANT: The Unstructured API uses:\\n- POST to https://transform.unstructured.io/api/v2/parse\\n- Header: unstructured-api-key\\n- Form data: profile=best, output=elements  \\n- File upload: input=(filename, content, 'application/pdf')\\n- Response may be\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation."}
